# Copy to .env and adjust. Every variable here is parsed and validated by Zod when
# the app loads (apps/web/src/config/env.ts). A malformed value fails fast with a
# message naming the variable.
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables are exposed to the browser bundle, and Vite
# inlines them at BUILD time. Never put a secret behind a VITE_ prefix — it ships
# to every user.
#
# No variables are required.

# GitHub App sign-in (FR-2.5, ADR-0016). Optional: set BOTH to enable it; with either
# empty the "Sign in with GitHub App" button is shown disabled and PAT sign-in is the only way.
# The App's client id (`Iv1.…` or `Iv23…`, from the App's settings page). Public, not a secret.
VITE_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# The exchange handler that holds the App's secret and trades a code or refresh token for
# tokens (docs/architecture/github-app-exchange.md). Must be https:, except
# http://localhost or http://127.0.0.1 for local development. Its origin joins the CSP
# connect-src when the Docker image is built with the same value.
VITE_GITHUB_APP_EXCHANGE_URL=
